From 997a84c8cc7969026866d15294e7edda3d41dc32 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rogan Lynch <roganl@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 07:26:21 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] source: mark source file handles close-on-exec

A source keeps its FILE open until it is freed, which for the
sources of a loaded program is the lifetime of the process. Without
FD_CLOEXEC these handles survive execve(), so a process that
re-execs itself with the program still loaded (rpcd on SIGHUP)
carries every previous generation along: one descriptor per ucode
source file per reload, until RLIMIT_NOFILE is hit.

Set FD_CLOEXEC after opening the file.

Newer ucode (1dd1f88, "close the file of a source after its
compilation") no longer holds the handle open; this is the minimal
equivalent for the release pinned by openwrt-25.12.

Signed-off-by: Rogan Lynch <roganl@gmail.com>
---
 source.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

--- a/source.c
+++ b/source.c
@@ -16,6 +16,7 @@
 
 #include <string.h>
 #include <errno.h>
+#include <fcntl.h>
 
 #include "ucode/source.h"
 #include "ucode/platform.h"
@@ -30,6 +31,9 @@ uc_source_new_file(const char *path)
 	if (!fp)
 		return NULL;
 
+	/* the handle stays open until the source is freed, keep it out of exec()ed images */
+	fcntl(fileno(fp), F_SETFD, FD_CLOEXEC);
+
 	src = xalloc(ALIGN(sizeof(*src)) + strlen(path) + 1);
 
 	src->header.type = UC_SOURCE;
